    "label": {
      "en": "Region Galicia: rate 1"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tin_rg11_rate1"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "First-bracket rate (9%) of the regional 'escala autonómica' that Galicia applies to its share of general (non-savings) personal income tax, one of up to ten region-specific bracket-rate constants ($tin_rg11_rate1…rate10) defined in tin_cons_es for this Autonomous Community. An ArithOp formula in tin_cons_es (output v_tin_ts_rt1_rg) multiplies every region's own rate-1 constant by that region's residence indicator (i_reg_11 for Galicia) and sums across all ~19 Spanish regions, so a Galician taxpayer's 9% rate is the one actually selected. The resulting v_tin_ts_rt1_rg variable is then used as the bracket-1 rate in the 'Regional Tax schedule on general income (cuota 2 general autonómica)' SchedCalc run within the individual- and joint-taxation policies (tinit_es, tinjt_es)."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Tax Schedule - Galicia"
    },
